ect** using a lightweight ZIP writer, with story JSON and assets included, plus Gradle wrapper? That is an APK build kit. Then offer prebuilt APK separately. However \"со сборкой в апк\" likely happy with prebuilt and build pipeline.\n\nMaybe implement cloud build simulation not accepted. We can actually run a local build server? Deployment is static only. Could use `npm run build:apk -- --story ...` but web cannot write files. Static build with Vite pre-builds current demo. Fine.\n\nCould create **APK build pipeline**: `scripts/build-apk.mjs` reads `public/story.json` and bundles into Android WebView project, compiles with Gradle, outputs `public/downloads/echo7.apk`. It proves actual APK. Include docs. Also app \"Сборка\" provides command; maybe user downloads.\n\nNeed perhaps modify `start.sh`? It already runs runtime default using package project; if Vite present, it builds dist and serves. Good. But our built APK in `public/downloads` will be copied to dist if under public. If built APK path is current story. Need generate before start/build, but Vite copies public existing. We can build APK once and commit artifact. Start rebuilds dist and copies.\n\nNeed be careful file size. APK minimal maybe 1-2 MB. Fine.\n\nNeed package.json. Use React 19? Vite 7 maybe Node 24 fine. Let's install after files.\n\nVisual details:\n- Fonts: Need offline. Use Google Fonts maybe network unavailable. We can bundle WOFF2 from Google Fonts via download. Use `@font-face` local. We can fetch fonts: \"Unbounded\" (display, Cyrillic), \"Manrope\" (body, Cyrillic), \"Cormorant Garamond\" maybe for title. Need Cyrillic. Download WOFF2 via fonts.googleapis.com. Let's test internet and fetch. We can use `curl`. Could install npm packages, network likely. Let's check.","native":{"reasoningField":"reasoning_content"},"time":{"created":1794204369134,"completed":1794204396577}},{"type":"tool","id":"call_5af8f5518930490084154a84","name":"shell","executed":false,"state":{"status":"completed","i