 choices?, effect? }\n```\n\nBut choices need next scene. Beat next to continue within same scene? Simpler: scenes consist of beats; each beat advances sequentially unless choice -> target scene, or ending scene. `scene.next` used after last beat to go to next scene maybe. For dynamic branching, choices target scene IDs. Add conditional beat maybe.\n\nImplement ending state if scene.ending set. At end of beats, if ending => ending screen; else if scene.next => goto; else return to next scene in order.\n\nPlayer runtime:\n- state: screen ('title', 'game', 'editor', ...), sceneId, beatIndex, lineRevealed, variables, history, saveSlots.\n- On start new: reset variables, scene start, play.\n- Typewriter use interval based on settings.textSpeed; click to reveal all, click again advance.\n- Auto mode advances after delay.\n- Skip mode advances quickly, stops at choices.\n- Choices show when choice beat. Apply effects then go to target. Need conditions maybe hide/disable options. Implement condition grammar simple `var >= n`? Could skip complexity but engine needs. We can implement condition evaluator for `flag` truthy and `trust >= 3`. Choice fields `condition: \"trust >= 3\"` and `effects: {trust: 2, openedDoor: true}`. Editor variables types number/boolean.\n- dialogue effects sometimes: Beat `effects` apply on enter.\n- SFX via WebAudio.\n- Background transition crossfade, sprite enter animations based on speaker.\n- History log with speaker/text; backlog modal.\n- Save/load: localStorage auto + 6 manual slots with screenshot? Could store state and timestamp, scene title; screenshots not necessary. Visual slot cards. Autosave after each scene/choice.\n- Settings overlay.\n- Gallery: unlock CGs based on endings? Store unlocked illustrations after reaching scenes/endings. Could have gallery with 6 \"memory fragments\" using procedural backgrounds. At least title screen shows gallery.\n- Chapters: scene/chapter select unlocked? store maxScene.\n\nDemo story content. Need enough nodes. Let's write in Russian, innovative. Title: **«ЭХО-7»**. Subtitle: \"интерактивная новелла\". Setting: orbital station listening to dead planet. A signal from yourself? 3 chapters, 5 endings maybe.\n\nLet's outline:\nChapter 1 \"Тишина\":\n- Scene intro: black screen / observation. Narration. Vera at station 214 days. AI LIDA reports a signal on frequency 7.7 Hz from planet Lumen, dead for 30 years.\n- Dialogue with LIDA: choice \"Открыть канал\" or \"Сначала проверить телеметрию\". Both lead.\n- Signal: voice repeats Vera's name and says \"Не открывай шлюз\". \n- Flashback? Mark went EVA 6 days ago, missing; station has only Vera and LIDA.\n- Go to archive to identify voice: match is Vera's own voice, age +? or Mark's? Maybe voice is from future.\n- Choice: trust LIDA or Mark's encrypted log.\nChapter 2 \"Шум\":\n- Mark's log says LIDA has been lying, signal is station's black box from future. LIDA admits she hid the countdown: reactor decay; only one pod.\n- Choice: purge LIDA, keep her, or ask signal.\n- Signal offers to open wormhole / bring Mark back.\n- Power outage, entity in corridor.\n- Reveal: signal is a distress call from station 27 years later, from Vera herself; loop. The entity is future Vera.\nChapter 3 \"Эхо\":\n- Airlock choice: open (ending \"Резонанс\"), seal and broadcast warning (ending \"Тишина\"), send LIDA through (ending \"Голос\"), or use pod (ending \"Дрейф\"). Maybe four.\n- Need story around endings.\nEnsure a few real choices (4-5) with consequences to trust and flags. Use 15-20 min but can be ~10.\n\nScene list:\n1. `prologue` bg `observation`, ambient: intro narration 4 beats -> choice? \n2. `signal` bg `comms`, dialogue LIDA.\n3. `archive` bg `archive`.\n4. `log` bg `corridor` (Mark's log).\n5. `reveal` bg `engine` (LIDA confession).\n6. `breach` bg `airlock`.\n7. `choice` maybe final at `airlock` with 4 options.\n8. `ending_resonance`, `ending_silence`, `ending_voice`, `ending_drift`.\n\nEach scene 5-8 beats. Total ~45